{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772652843,"nonce":"iF3bXVl+tJLmxxzggTxuWhqqkbA=","title":"Mandible UI: show rebuilding/restarting splash on self-merge","message":"When Mandible detects it is merging a commit into its own protected branch (main), it should:\n\n1. Immediately show a full-page 'Rebuilding \u0026 restarting...' notice in the UI before the restart begins\n2. Disconnect SSE / stop rendering the normal UI so there are no confusing partial states\n3. Poll /api/health after restart begins; auto-reload the page when the server is back up\n\nThis avoids the jarring experience of the UI going dead mid-interaction without explanation.\n\nThe trigger is available via SSE or the auth-executor knowing the target is the Mandible repo itself. The simplest approach may be a dedicated SSE event (e.g. `mandible:rebuilding`) emitted by auth-executor just before it kicks off the restart, which the UI listens for.\n\nUser context: came up when merging a fix to auth-executor itself caused Mandible to restart mid-session, leaving the UI in a confusing state.","files":null}]}